README-X68K -- programs for the Sharp X68000's personal-window systemOS-9/X68000 ran on Sharp's X68000 and had a windowing system of its own,the "personal window" (PW/X), reached through the /win device.  These twoprograms were written for it by Masahiko Ito (as WADACHI on NIFTY-Serve),1991-92.  WE CANNOT TEST THEM: there is no X68000 and no /win here.  Askedto start, x9eyes answers `PwCreateMap error' and setbgptn `can't open /win'.  x9eyes     xeyes for the personal window: two eyes that follow the             pointer, and the window can be resized.  -t<tick> sets how             often it redraws; -g<width>x<height> sets the size (1.04,             1992-12-10).  setbgptn   sets the window system's background pattern from a file of             16 lines of 16 characters, a space for a clear dot and             anything else for a set one.  The archive has four:             BLACK.BGP, BLOCK.BGP, DEFAULT.BGP and X.BGP.Both need cio.THE ARCHIVES SHIP WHOLE, in CMDS/archives, and that is a condition oftheir terms.  x9eyes.doc: "(1) Please do not change the contents of theoriginal archive.  (2) Please tell the author, where possible, where it hasbeen distributed."  PwLib.doc, for the library both are built on: "Feelfree to redistribute provided that 1. the author's credits are notremoved, and 2. the composition of the archive is not changed -- additionsby the distributor are allowed."  Their documentation is in Japanese, inShift-JIS, which this disk cannot carry as text; it is inside thearchives, unchanged.  This file is a distributor's addition.The archives are the author's own 2018 re-release (dated 2018-09-11) ofthis 1991-92 work.  setbgptn's still carries the 1991 library; x9eyes'scarries the library as re-released in 2018, and the binary is the one inthat archive.